###### Abstract

Several open inequalities for ratios and logarithmic derivatives of the modified Bessel functions I_{
u} of the first kind and K_{
u} of the second kind reduce to sign questions for quadratic Riccati expressions. We isolate this reduction and use it in two directions. First, for the quotient W_{
u}(z)=zI_{
u}(z)/I_{
u+1}(z), the canonical product for I_{
u+1} yields the partial fraction W_{
u}(\sqrt{s})=2(
u+1)+2\sum_{n\geq 1}s/(s+j_{
u+1,n}^{2}), where j_{
u+1,n} is the n-th positive zero of J_{
u+1}. Consequently x\mapsto W_{
u}(x^{	au}) is a Bernstein function for 
u>-1 and 0<	au\leq 1/2, and this positive exponent range is sharp. Second, an exact rational certificate at (
u,u)=(0,10) places I_{1}(10)/I_{0}(10) below 0.949. This refutes the log-concavity question of Baricz, Ponnusamy, and Vuorinen for u\mapsto\sqrt{u}\,I_{
u}(u) and its displayed Riccati reformulations. The same framework completes the monotonicity classification of K_{
u}^{\prime}/K_{
u}^{2}, refutes Baricz–Ponnusamy–Vuorinen Question 7 at 
u=1/2, and gives an entire counterexample to Baricz’s coefficient-ratio complete-monotonicity transfer problem.

###### Keywords:

modified Bessel functions , Bernstein functions , completely monotone functions , logarithmic concavity , Turán-type inequalities , Riccati equations

###### 2020 MSC

33C10 , 26A48 , 26A51 , 26D07 , 44A10 , 60G51

