4 One certificate for log-concavity

Question 1 of Baricz, Ponnusamy, and Vuorinen (BPV) asks whether $u\mapsto\sqrt{u},I_{
u}(u)$ is strictly log-concave on $(0,\infty)$ for every $
u\geq 0$ [ 5 , Question 1] . Lemma 2.4 identifies this question with the sign of the Riccati expression ( 8 ), and with the corresponding quadratic lower bound for the ratio $q_{
u}=I_{
u+1}/I_{
u}$ . A later coefficient-based treatment discusses log-concavity statements for $t^{\mu}I_{
u}(t)$ , including the square-root case $(
u,\mu)=(0,1/2)$ [ 20 , Theorem 4] . The certificate below gives an exact obstruction at $
u=0$ . Thus the single certificate stated in Lemma 4.1 , with the arithmetic isolated in Appendix A , refutes the BPV source question and the two algebraic reformulations displayed below.

